emulators/virtualbox-ose-additions-72: rewrite the vboxvfs shared folder driver

Replace the shared folder file system driver (vboxvfs.ko) and
mount_vboxvfs(8) that the port carried as patches on top of the upstream
stubs with a new implementation written from scratch for FreeBSD 15.x
and 16-CURRENT.  The old driver dated from 2008 and was never adapted
to the vnode and buffer cache interfaces of recent FreeBSD: it leaked
the parent's vnode lock on ".." lookups, rename always failed with
ENOENT, every file reported mode 0755, the kernel panicked at mount
time on INVARIANTS kernels, and two pjdfstest cases locked the system
up.

The new driver follows the NFS and smbfs model:

- a node cache keyed by (parent, name) with vfs_hash(9), inode numbers
  from a hash of the path, and a name cache with a ttl (mount option
  "ttl", default 200 ms) behind which host side changes are picked up;
- read/write/mmap through the buffer cache with 64 KiB blocks, pages
  handed to the host directly (HGCM page lists, no copying), write
  through, and VOP_GETPAGES via vfs_bio_getpages(9) so that mmap and
  read(2)/write(2) share the same pages;
- rename, rmdir and remove integrated with the name cache
  (cache_vop_rename(9), cache_vop_rmdir(9)), unlinked files stay usable
  while open;
- mode, times and ownership mapped to the host with the usual
  uid/gid/file_mode/dir_mode/fmask/dmask mount options; symbolic links
  are shown and created when the share allows it.

Tested with pjdfstest on 15.1-RELEASE and 16-CURRENT (INVARIANTS,
WITNESS): 171 of 238 test files pass completely; the remaining failures
are limits of the shared folder protocol and host side policy (no
device nodes, fifos, sockets or hard links, chown ignored, the host
forcing the owner read bit and clearing setuid/setgid/sticky, path
length limits), the same set the Linux vboxsf client fails.  fsx with
mmap, a 10 minute mixed stress run (fsx, stress2, a copy/diff/git
workload and concurrent changes from the host) and 2 hours of operation
showed no panics, lockups or data mismatches.

The sources are dual licensed GPL-3.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause and are
maintained at https://github.com/lwhsu/freebsd-vboxfs; the patches in
this commit are generated from that tree by ports/gen-ports-patch.sh.
The man page is installed now, and pkg-message tells how to mount a
share.

